Proper response is "I do." :D Unless you drink your coffee with neither...

Also, that would depend on the waiter's emphasis of the sentence:


"Do you want CREAM or SUGAR in your coffee?"

means:

"Is this true: (You want cream in your coffee. =E2=8A=95 You want sugar in =
your
coffee.)?"


"Do you WANT cream or sugar in your coffee?"

means:

"Is this true: (You want cream in your coffee. =E2=88=A8 You want sugar in =
your
coffee.)?"




("=E2=8A=95" is XOR, "=E2=88=A8" is OR.)



So presuming the waiter emphasised "cream" and "sugar", not "want", "yes" o=
r
"I do" are not proper responses.

